2026-03-28 02:42:29 - Agent_20260328024147 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 9 CodeQL queries all pointing to a Zip Slip vulnerability in `InputStreamHelper.java`. Confirmed a single critical true positive: the `processZipStream` method constructs a `File` object at line 126 using `ZipEntry.getName()` without any path traversal validation, then writes to it via `FileOutputStream` at line 139. There is no canonicalization, no containment check, no filtering of `../` sequences anywhere in the method. The public entry point `writeZipStreamToTempDir` makes this directly exploitable by any caller passing a malicious ZIP stream. Submitted 1 finding (true positive, critical severity, CWE-022).
